-- N5 example sentences, batch 12: greetings and the set phrases.
--
-- ありがとうございます was coming apart as あり | が | と | う | ご | ざ | います —
-- seven pieces, one of them the verb 居る, for the first phrase anybody learns.
-- JMdict is not wrong to leave it out; it is 有り難う plus ございます, each with
-- its own entry, and the polite form is generated rather than listed. But a
-- beginner meets it as one thing, and the greetings lesson is about the phrase.
--
-- These are the expressions where the pieces are less useful than the whole.
-- Everything else stays decomposed: 本を読んで、書いてください is a request built
-- out of parts a reader should learn to see, and gluing it together teaches
-- less, so the 〜て chain topic keeps its pieces.
--
-- Additive, idempotent, safe on a live database.

  -- greetings
  ('sent-ex-greet-1', 'lang-ja', 'おはようございます。', 'おはようございます。', 'lvl-ja-n5', 'authored', true),
  ('sent-ex-greet-2', 'lang-ja', 'こんにちは。', 'こんにちは。', 'lvl-ja-n5', 'authored', true),
  ('sent-ex-greet-3', 'lang-ja', 'こんばんは。', 'こんばんは。', 'lvl-ja-n5', 'authored', true),
  ('sent-ex-greet-4', 'lang-ja', 'さようなら。', 'さようなら。', 'lvl-ja-n5', 'authored', true),
  -- sumimasen
